# Local overrides for development. Copy to .env.local (gitignored).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE AT ALL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Configuration lives in ONE place now:
#
#     config/app.config.ts
#
# — which model reads a photo, where the Worker is, upload size, timeouts.
# Both the React app and the Cloudflare Worker import it, so there is one
# answer rather than two that drift. Change it there, not here.
#
# The only reason to use this file is to point a local build at a DIFFERENT
# worker than the configured one — testing a preview deploy, say.
#
# VITE_IMAGE_PROXY_URL=https://some-other-worker.workers.dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO API KEY GOES IN THIS FILE. NOT EVER.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Not OPENROUTER_API_KEY, not GEMINI_API_KEY. Two independent reasons:
#
# 1. It would not work. This file is read by Vite, which builds the FRONTEND.
#    The Cloudflare Worker is a separate program on a separate machine and
#    never sees it.
#
# 2. It would leak the key. Anything Vite exposes is compiled into the public
#    JS bundle and served to every visitor, and this repo is public. Keeping
#    the key out of the browser is the entire reason the Worker exists.
#
# Keys are Worker secrets. From cf-worker/:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   npx wrangler secret put GEMINI_API_KEY
#
# It prompts for the value, encrypts it at Cloudflare, and writes nothing to
# disk. config/app.config.ts lists both names under `secrets`, so that is still
# the one place to LOOK — only the values live elsewhere, as they must.
